{
    "comment": [
        "Applications that can be packaged for a mobile platform, and the identity each one ships",
        "under. This file is the single source of truth for three consumers that used to hard-code",
        "gkNextRenderer: src/cmake/MobileApplications.cmake (which application directory a mobile",
        "configure adds), tools/android (applicationId and launcher label baked into the APK), and",
        "gnb (the --app flag of `gnb android` and `gnb ios`).",
        "",
        "An application that is absent from this list is desktop-only; nothing else marks it as such.",
        "",
        "Fields:",
        "  target          CMake target name, and the name passed to --app.",
        "  directory       Application directory, relative to src/Application. A mobile configure adds",
        "                  exactly this one directory, so it has to be self-contained.",
        "  label           Launcher / bundle display name.",
        "  platforms       Which mobile platforms can package it.",
        "  androidId       applicationId of the APK. Distinct per application so one device can hold",
        "                  more than one of them at a time.",
        "  iosBundleId     Bundle identifier of the .app. Must match an installed provisioning profile;",
        "                  see the note in gk_configure_ios_application about never reusing an",
        "                  identifier another Apple team has already shipped.",
        "  requiresDotNet  The application hosts C#, so it can only be configured where the managed",
        "                  scripting layer exists (Android NativeAOT; never iOS)."
    ],
    "applications": [
        {
            "target": "gkNextRenderer",
            "directory": "Render/gkNextRenderer",
            "label": "gkNextRenderer",
            "platforms": ["android", "ios"],
            "androidId": "com.gknext.renderer",
            "iosBundleId": "gknext.renderer"
